From f7b6147767b826ede6dc8136e1e9bdb26c9c32a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ExposureMG <exposuremg@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] RK3588Dxe: power on the Mali-G610 GPU at boot

Windows has no Rockchip power-domain driver, and TF-A only powers PD_GPU
around system suspend, so GPU registers would raise an SError when read.
Add a "GPU" setup page (GpuState, default enabled) and, when enabled:

1. set clk_gpu to 200 MHz via SCMI (direct CRU fallback: GPLL/6),
2. ungate the GPU clocks in CRU CLKGATE_CON66/67 and release the GPU
   resets in SOFTRST_CON66/67,
3. power on PD_GPU (PMU2 PWR_GATE_SFTCON0 bit0) and wait for the memory
   repair status (BISR_STATUS4 bit1),
4. release the GPU NIU idle request (BUS_IDLE_SFTCON0 bit0) and wait for
   ACK/status to clear,
5. log GPU_ID.

The sequence runs only once vdd_gpu_s0 has been configured by
Rk806Configure() and the setup variables are applied, whichever comes
last. AcpiPlatformDxe sets \_SB.GPU0._STA to 0 when the GPU is disabled.

Register meaning cross-checked against TF-A (BSD-3-Clause) pmu.c and
rk3588_clk.c. Untested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
